# Paths the handbook checks skip, one per line: a glob, or `kind: glob`.
# A bare glob skips the path in every check; `orphan:` exempts it from the
# orphan check alone, and `em-dash:` from the em dash check alone. A trailing /
# covers everything below, and * spans directory separators. Write the reason
# beside each line, and delete what does not apply here.
# Handbook: /handbook/meta/local/README.md says what this repository does not
# author, and the shared rules say what needs no backreference; both belong
# here, by kind.

# The vendored engine is upstream's; what this repository changes about it is
# the patch stack under patch/.
src/duckdb/

# Generated documents cannot carry a backreference; the generator does.
orphan: NEWS.md
orphan: tests/testthat/_snaps/
orphan: revdep/

# The two rendered READMEs come from README.Rmd and are read from a tarball
# that does not carry handbook/, so their pointer into the tree is a full URL
# rather than a link the checks can resolve.
orphan: README.md
orphan: .github/README.md

# The no-em-dash rule is on the local page and binds what is written from now
# on. The tree predates it, so the check stays off until a sweep clears what is
# already there.
em-dash: *
